{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"986","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Perfect Encoding"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are working as an analyst in a company working on a new system for big data storage. This system will store $$$n$$$ different objects. Each object should have a unique ID."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To create the system, you choose the parameters of the system — integers $$$m \\ge 1$$$ and $$$b_{1}, b_{2}, \\ldots, b_{m}$$$. With these parameters an ID of some object in the system is an array of integers $$$[a_{1}, a_{2}, \\ldots, a_{m}]$$$ where $$$1 \\le a_{i} \\le b_{i}$$$ holds for every $$$1 \\le i \\le m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Developers say that production costs are proportional to $$$\\sum_{i=1}^{m} b_{i}$$$. You are asked to choose parameters $$$m$$$ and $$$b_{i}$$$ so that the system will be able to assign unique IDs to $$$n$$$ different objects and production costs are minimized. Note that you don't have to use all available IDs."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the only line of input there is one positive integer $$$n$$$. The length of the decimal representation of $$$n$$$ is no greater than $$$1.5 \\cdot 10^{6}$$$. The integer does not contain leading zeros."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one number — minimal value of $$$\\sum_{i=1}^{m} b_{i}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"36\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"37\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"11\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12345678901234567890123456789\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"177\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"986D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/986/problem/D"}